{
  "id": "regression-house-prices",
  "title": "House prices — multiple regression as a path model (SYNTHETIC)",
  "summary": "Sale price regressed on living area, building age, distance to the centre and a garage dummy. A multiple regression is a path model with one outcome. Synthetic data (N = 300).",
  "theory": "Hedonic pricing: a dwelling's price reflects the value of its characteristics (Rosen, 1974, Journal of Political Economy, 82(1), 34–55). Used here only as a familiar regression setting.",
  "modelNote": "CB-SEM ML gives unstandardised slopes in the variables' own units (thousand EUR per m², per year, per km, and for having a garage); they equal the OLS slopes. Standard errors differ slightly from OLS because ML divides by N. The model is just-identified (df = 0), so global fit is not informative.",
  "scaleSource": "Price in thousand EUR; area in m²; age in years; distance in km; garage coded 0/1.",
